  "legalOwnerReview": "Draft wording — to be confirmed by Melai Nuts.",
  "legalSection": "LEGAL",
  "legalTermsSubtitle": "Rules for using the app",
  "legalPrivacySubtitle": "What data we collect and your rights",
  "termsS1Title": "1. What this app does",
  "termsS1Body": "Melai Nuts lets you browse products, order from a Melai Nuts branch for pickup at the counter, track your orders, request refunds and earn loyalty points. Staff and owners use the same app for the shop counter and stock.",
  "termsS2Title": "2. Your account",
  "termsS2Body": "Give your real name, a working email and a mobile number you own. Before your first order you verify that number with a 6-digit code we send by SMS; one number can belong to only one Melai Nuts account. Keep your password secret and do not share your account. You are responsible for what is done with your account. Tell a branch right away if you think someone else is using it. We may deactivate an account that breaks these terms.",
  "termsS3Title": "3. Orders and payment",
  "termsS3Body": "Prices, stock and discounts are checked by our system when you place the order; the total on your confirmation is the amount you pay. Orders are for pickup at the branch counter.\n• Your first order: you pay 50% or 100% of it online through HitPay (GCash, QR Ph or card) before the branch prepares it. If you pay 50%, you can pay the other 50% online later in the app or on the website, or in cash when you pick up. This rule applies to every new account and every mobile number that has not had an order paid online yet.\n• Later orders: when online payment is on, you pay the downpayment shown at checkout online and the rest in cash when you pick up. When online payment is off, you pay the full amount in cash at pickup.\n• Only HitPay's own confirmation marks a payment as paid automatically. If HitPay's confirmation does not reach us, the owner may confirm your payment by hand after checking HitPay's records. Your order then goes ahead, but your next order still counts as a first order until a payment is confirmed by HitPay.\n• An order may be cancelled if an item runs out; you are not charged for cancelled items.",
  "termsS4Title": "4. Refunds",
  "termsS4Body": "You can ask for a refund in the app, with a reason, within 7 days after you pick up your order. The branch reviews each request. The refund amount is computed by the system from the items you return, not typed in by anyone. Approved refunds are paid back in cash at the branch or to the original payment method.",
  "termsS5Title": "5. Loyalty points",
  "termsS5Body": "You earn points when an order is completed. Points from an order that is refunded are taken back. Points have no cash value, cannot be transferred to another person and are used only for rewards in this app. Melai Nuts may change the earning and reward rules; changes are shown in the app at least 30 days before they apply.",
  "termsS6Title": "6. Pickup, online payment and downpayment",
  "termsS6Body": "• Pay the online part of your order (first-order payment or downpayment) within the time shown at checkout, 30 minutes unless the shop sets another limit. If it is not paid in time, the order is cancelled and nothing is charged.\n• Pick up your order within 2 days after it is marked \"Ready for Pickup\". If you do not pick it up in time, the order is cancelled and the shop keeps the downpayment.\n• If the order is cancelled for any other reason, including by the shop, the money you paid online is refunded in full to the payment method you used.\n• Pay any balance online in the app or on the website before pickup, or in cash at the counter when you pick up. If a balance is paid both online and in cash, the online payment is refunded.",
  "termsS7Title": "7. Acceptable use",
  "termsS7Body": "Do not place orders you do not mean to pay for or collect, use a mobile number that is not yours, create extra accounts to avoid the first-order payment, guess voucher codes, copy the catalog with automated tools, try to get around the app's security, or use another person's account. The app limits repeated attempts to protect every customer: after many failed sign-ins it asks for a security check (Cloudflare Turnstile) before you can try again.",
  "termsS8Title": "8. Changes to these terms",
  "termsS8Body": "When these terms or the Privacy Policy change, the app shows the new version and asks you to accept it again before you continue.",
  "termsS9Title": "9. Contact",
  "termsS9Body": "For questions about your account, an order or these terms, contact any Melai Nuts branch or email melaioraya5@gmail.com. Branch phone numbers are shown in the app on the order details and checkout screens. Business details: [TO BE FILLED IN BY THE OWNER: registered business name and business address].",
  "privacyS1Title": "1. Who is responsible for your data",
  "privacyS1Body": "Melai Nuts Retailing ([TO BE FILLED IN BY THE OWNER: registered business name and business address]) is the personal information controller for the data in this app and on the Melai Nuts website, as defined by the Philippine Data Privacy Act of 2012 (Republic Act No. 10173). Our Data Protection Officer is the owner of Melai Nuts Retailing, reachable at melaioraya5@gmail.com.",
  "privacyS2Title": "2. Data we collect",
  "privacyS2Body": "• Your name, email address and mobile number. Your mobile number is verified with an SMS code; the database keeps the verified number and when it was verified.\n• Your orders, payments, refunds and loyalty points, including which of your orders was your first order paid online, and the mobile number it was paid with.\n• When the owner confirms a payment by hand: the reason, the payment reference and which owner account confirmed it.\n• Sign-in protection: the email address you sign in with, the IP address of your connection and an ID of your device, each stored only as a keyed one-way hash (not readable as an address or number), with the time of each attempt.\n• The 6-digit email codes we send when you create an account, stored only as a keyed one-way hash.\n• Your phone's location, used on your phone (or in your browser, only after you agree) to choose the nearest open branch. We save only the branch, not your location.\n• A notification token so we can send order updates to this phone.\n• Crash reports, which carry an account ID but not your name, email or phone.",
  "privacyS3Title": "3. How we use it",
  "privacyS3Body": "To create your account and verify your email and mobile number, prepare your orders, take payment, apply the first-order payment rule (so a new account cannot use another customer's number to skip it), handle refunds, keep your loyalty points, send the updates you chose, protect sign-in against password guessing, keep the app secure, and fix problems. We do not sell your data.",
  "privacyS4Title": "4. Where it is stored and who can see it",
  "privacyS4Body": "• Firebase (Google): sign-in (your account ID and password check), the SMS codes that verify your mobile number, App Check (confirms requests come from the real Melai Nuts app), push notifications and crash reports.\n• Supabase: our database, file storage and server functions, where your business data is kept.\n• Resend: sends Melai Nuts account emails: the 6-digit codes, password-reset and email-change links, and security notices.\n• Cloudflare Turnstile: the security check shown when you create an account and after repeated failed sign-ins.\n• Google reCAPTCHA: the security check before the website sends a code to your mobile number.\n• HitPay: online payments. We receive the payment status, amount and method, not your card or GCash details.\n• OpenStreetMap: the map tiles in the app.\nA copy of recent data is kept on your phone so the app works offline; it is erased when you sign out. Staff see only what their branch needs.",
  "privacyS5Title": "5. How long we keep it",
  "privacyS5Body": "Orders, payments, refunds, manual payment confirmations and the record of which mobile number paid a first order are kept for 5 years for tax and accounting records and to apply the first-order rule. Email codes expire after 10 minutes and the record of sent codes is deleted after 1 day. Password-reset links expire after 30 minutes and email-change links after 1 hour; each works once, only a scrambled form of it is stored, and it is deleted after 7 days. Sign-in attempt records are deleted after 1 day, and a successful sign-in clears the ones for your email and device sooner. Account details are kept while your account is active and are deleted within 30 days of a deletion request, except records we must keep by law.",
  "privacyS6Title": "6. Your rights (RA 10173)",
  "privacyS6Body": "You have the right to be informed, to access your data, to object, to have it corrected, to have it erased or blocked, to data portability, to claim damages, and to file a complaint with the National Privacy Commission (privacy.gov.ph).",
  "privacyS7Title": "7. Deleting your data",
  "privacyS7Body": "To ask for a copy of your data, to have your account deleted, or with any other privacy question, email melaioraya5@gmail.com. Account details are deleted within 30 days of the request. Records the law requires us to keep (for example, receipts) are kept but no longer linked to your profile where possible.",
  "privacyS8Title": "8. Permissions on your phone",
  "privacyS8Body": "The app asks for the camera (scan barcodes) and notifications (order updates) only when you use that feature. Location: when you open the app or the web shop (once per visit) and at checkout, we ask for your location to find your nearest pickup branch. Your position is used once to pick the branch and is not stored; we keep only the chosen branch and its distance. If you say no, or location is off, you choose your branch from a list and can still check out. It does not ask for permission to read your SMS: on Android the code may be filled in for you by Google's SMS Retriever, which shares only the one message with the code. You can change permissions any time in Settings > Permissions.",
  "privacyS9Title": "9. Product photos and file access",
  "privacyS9Body": "• What we collect: the product photos the Melai Nuts owner chooses on the admin website, with each photo's file type, size and upload time, the product it belongs to, and the owner account that uploaded it. Only the owner uploads product photos; customers do not.\n• Why: to show the products to customers in the Melai Nuts app and the web shop.\n• File access: the website reads only the photo files the owner picks in the browser's file picker (or drags onto the page). It does not scan or read any other files or folders on the device. The owner first allows file access with the \"Allow photo access\" button; the website records that owner's choice and when it was made, and the owner can reset it at any time.\n• Where they are stored: in Supabase Storage, in the public \"product-images\" folder. Anyone with a photo's link can view it, so private or personal photos must not be uploaded.\n• Large photos are resized in the browser before they are uploaded.\n• The owner can remove or replace photos at any time. Removed and replaced photos are deleted from storage.\n• Questions about product photos: email melaioraya5@gmail.com.",
  "privacyS10Title": "10. Your mobile number and the first-order rule",
  "privacyS10Body": "• We send a 6-digit code to the number you enter, through Firebase. The number counts as verified only after you enter the right code; a number you type anywhere else (for example as a contact number) does not count.\n• A verified number can belong to only one Melai Nuts account at a time. If it is already verified on another account, it is refused.\n• We use the verified number to apply the first-order payment rule: a new account always pays its first order online first, whatever number it uses, and the number that paid a first order is recorded so it cannot be used to skip the rule on another account.\n• Staff use your verified number to reach you about a pickup order.",
  "privacyS11Title": "11. Security checks and sign-in protection",
  "privacyS11Body": "• Every sign-in attempt is counted by email address, IP address and device for 30 minutes. After 15 attempts, a security check (Cloudflare Turnstile) is needed before the next one. It never locks you out: a passed check always lets you try. The email, IP address and device ID are stored only as one-way hashes made with a secret key.\n• Cloudflare receives what it needs to run the security check (such as your IP address and browser details) under its own privacy policy. Google receives the same for reCAPTCHA on the website's mobile-number step.\n• App Check: the app proves to our servers that it is the genuine Melai Nuts app on a real device (Google Play Integrity or Apple App Attest). No personal data is added for this.\n• Password reset: the reset link in the email works once and expires; after the change, your other sign-ins are ended.",
